      ⍝ Bugs28 #37 regression: A∘.f B with an empty result kept only
      ⍝ the first *cell* of RO's fill result as Z's prototype (dropping
      ⍝ everything but that one cell/level for a non-scalar or nested
      ⍝ fill result), and never converted a wrong-VALUE fill result
      ⍝ (e.g. RO's own identity element) to a type-correct default.
      ⍝ Fixed in Bif_OPER2_OUTER.cc: set_ravel_Value() (copies the cell
      ⍝ for a simple scalar, else wraps in a fresh PointerCell, mirror-
      ⍝ ing EACH's own empty-fill logic) followed by to_type(false) --
      ⍝ NOT to_type(true) as EACH uses, since a user-defined RO's fill
      ⍝ result can legitimately be a character cell that must stay
      ⍝ character (a space), not get force-converted to numeric 0.
      ⍝
      X←0⍴⊂1 2
      Z←3∘.,X ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴(⊂3⍴0 0 0)

      ⍝ control: A f¨B on the same arguments was already correct
      Z←3,¨X ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴(⊂3⍴0 0 0)

