      ⍝ Bugs28 #57 regression (Bugs27 #56 residual): ∘.f (like ¨,
      ⍝ f⍤y, and f.g) still broke when the operand changed ⎕IO --
      ⍝ Z__A_LO_OUTER_B (Macro.def) indexed μ1/μ2/μ6, and even its own
      ⍝ cartesian-product index list μ10 (itself built by ⍳ under the
      ⍝ ORIGINAL ⎕IO), with the raw loop counter/disclosed indices,
      ⍝ seeded from ⎕IO ONCE at the start; if LO's own ⎕IO←0 (global,
      ⍝ not auto-localized in a lambda) persisted past its first call,
      ⍝ every later iteration misindexed instead of INDEX-ERROR-ing
      ⍝ outright. Fixed the same self-correcting way as the already-
      ⍝ fixed monadic ¨ (Z__LO_EACH_B): recompute ⎕IO+(offset-savedIO)
      ⍝ fresh at each use, for every index derived from that saved IO.
